{
  "name": "AI projects poised for greater impact",
  "parent_id": 203314470211128,
  "group_id": "145be208-94c3-433b-9cbf-a0dd53bb47e7",
  "alternates": [],
  "created_at": "2026-07-30T15:27:59.598Z",
  "deleted_at": null,
  "sort_by_date": null,
  "tag_list": [],
  "updated_at": "2026-08-12T15:14:47.650Z",
  "published_at": "2026-08-12T15:14:47.636Z",
  "id": 203717343662457,
  "uuid": "b704785b-40a1-4fc6-8548-9896c513204c",
  "is_folder": false,
  "content": {
    "_uid": "ef6f0ee3-2dfa-3124-dce0-dee8f7783544",
    "body": [
      {
        "_uid": "77b71e5b-0adb-0189-78e0-239755638865",
        "content": {
          "type": "doc",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Dr Alvi\ninformed faculty from the University's department of paediatrics and child\nhealth of the government's plans to harness the power of technology and\nprecision analytics to increase the quality of life of children across the\ncountry. The federal government is looking for promising projects that can\nbring healthcare to the doorstep of every child across the country via the\nnationwide Lady Health Worker Programme.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "The AKU\ndelegation presented a summary of the country's major health indicators at the meeting\nand pointed out how Pakistan needs to intensify efforts to reduce the incidence\nof neonatal mortality and lower the burden of infectious diseases. They also highlighted\nfindings from a World Bank report that lists Pakistan as one of the countries\nfacing a critical shortage of physicians, nurses and midwives.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "\"In order to\ngive Pakistan a fair chance of achieving the SDGs regarding health we need to\ntransform health systems using technology and artificial intelligence. This\ntransformation can happen via multiple pathways including workforce engagement,\nautomation of tasks, supervision and effective governance,\" said Dr Muneera\nRasheed, a senior instructor at AKU. \"These insights hold the potential to make\nwork comfortable, pleasurable and to create purpose-driven health systems.\"\n ",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Dr Babar\nHasan, an associate professor in paediatrics, briefed the president on how a\nteam of researchers* were using a machine learning model that uses ultrasounds\nto study blood flow to a foetus's crucial organs. The algorithm analyses images\nto determine markers of under-developed organs which can point towards babies\nat risk of stillbirth, perinatal mortality and other neonatal illnesses. ",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Dr Rasheed\nshared how researchers at the University** were using data from children in ER,\nthe emergency room, to improve the experience of young patients who would end\nup being admitted to the hospital. Machine learning, a type of artificial\nintelligence, is being used to analyse hospital data on patient demographics,\nwaiting times, billing details, average length of stay and customer surveys to\nforesee factors that impact patient satisfaction. Such insights can help\nimprove a hospital's understanding of patient expectations which can improve\ncommunication and provide a more positive experience for all parents and\npatients, said Dr Rasheed. ",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "At the end\nof the meeting, President Arif Alvi discussed the creation of a wide-ranging\nnational taskforce that would create a roadmap and develop partnerships on the\nuse of AI initiatives to achieve health targets under the SDGs.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "* ",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "text": "Dr Zahra\nHoodbhoy and Dr Fyezah Jehan are a part of the project research team.",
                  "type": "text",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "italic"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "** ",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "text": "Dr Momin\nKazi and Akbar Rajani are also part of this study.",
                  "type": "text",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "italic"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
